// seed.js — the proposed starting curriculum, A1 → C1.
//
// SOURCING: this is not lifted from any single app's internal unit list
// (no formal course publishes one at that granularity). It's built from the
// standard CEFR / Goethe-Institut topic-and-grammar progression that nearly
// every serious German course (Schritte international, Netzwerk, Aspekte,
// Goethe-Zertifikat exam syllabuses) follows — greetings before cases,
// Perfekt before Konjunktiv, etc. Vocab favors natural spoken phrasing
// ("Ich hätte gern...", "Hast du Lust auf...?") alongside the formal/
// textbook form where the two diverge, since the goal includes being able
// to actually hold a conversation in Germany or Austria, not just pass a
// written exam.
//
// This is a starting point, not a fixed syllabus -- everything here is fully
// editable in the Curriculum Editor afterward (rename, reorder, merge,
// delete, add). Treat the 40 units below as a strong skeleton to flesh out
// or rearrange, not a finished product.

